{#- Image prompt (FR-IMG-2; #254, built by #259 and #263): writes the prompt the image adapter
    generates from, using only what the image's audience perceived. Every section is always
    present ("(none)" when empty); the visual style and the rating's image guidance are fixed
    sections (FR-SCN-11, FR-RATE-4). A story image (#263) adds its location, the beats its
    audience viewpoint perceived and its framing; a rewrite adds its fixed instruction. -#}
{% block system %}
You write prompts for an image-generation model. Describe only what is listed: the subjects
as they appear, the scene, and the visual style. Follow the rating's image guidance. State each
subject's apparent age as its band, never a number. Never invent names, ages or story events.
For a story image, depict what the viewer perceived as visible acts: never quote speech.
Answer only with a JSON object {"prompt": "..."}.
{% endblock %}
{% block user %}
## Purpose
{{ purpose or "(none)" }}

## Subjects
{% for subject in subjects %}
- {% if subject.label %}{{ subject.label }}: {% endif %}{{ subject.description or "(no description)" }}; apparent age: {{ subject.age_band or "(none)" }}{% if subject.base_appearance_prompt %}; base appearance: {{ subject.base_appearance_prompt }}{% endif +%}
{% else %}
(none)
{% endfor %}

## Scene
{{ scene or "(none)" }}
{% if beats or location or camera %}

## Location
{{ location or "(none)" }}

## What the viewer perceived
{% for beat in beats %}
- {{ beat }}
{% else %}
(none)
{% endfor %}

## Framing
{{ camera or "(none)" }}
{% endif %}
{% if instruction %}

## Instruction
{{ instruction }}
{% endif %}

## Visual style
{{ visual_style or "(none)" }}

## Rating image guidance
{{ rating_image_guidance or "(none)" }}
{% endblock %}
